WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:03.940
Hi everybody! Tom here from BBC Learning English.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:07.249
Today I'm going to explain the difference

00:00:07.249 --> 00:00:11.170
between to steal to rob.

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:14.660
Both to steal and to rob mean

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.200
'to take something without permission'.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:22.060
To steal focuses on the object or the thing

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:25.200
which is taken. For example:

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:27.100
Hey!

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.080
Somebody just stole my phone.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:33.960
Rob focuses on the victim of the crime.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.340
For example:

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.190
The men robbed a bank last night.

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:40.940
I wouldn't say:

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.140
Someone robbed my phone.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:45.480
I would say:

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:50.200
They robbed me and stole my phone.

